# THE NEXT LIVE ENGINE, A CANDIDATE: ONE BUILD, ONE SWAP, ONE GATING OF EVERY
# RUN (operator, 2026-11-24, relayed by München: "I want it, and it is inside
# my "everything"" — the OmniVoice port becomes the speech backend; "I want
# the preemptive model load to be implemented and the MoE preloading in VRAM
# based on the recent experts used"; and, of the first sentence in a voice,
# "didn't we optimize it?"). Agreed with the architecture session as one
# build rather than one per feature: a new engine costs every vega run its
# gate again.
#   SERIES_FILE=deploy/localai/patches/staged/engine-next.series \
#     sh deploy/localai/llama-cpp/build.sh sycl_f16 <out dir>      # the live INTEL_STACK
# The live series, then, in the order they apply:
#   0009  OmniVoice on llama.cpp's own audio generation, with a voice clip's
#         encoding kept in a file the caller names
#   0010  LocalAI's speech call: a profile's transcript, a described voice,
#         seed / steps / guidance, and the kept encoding placed beside the
#         profile's own clip (gone with LocalAI's delete of the profile)
#   0012  GGML_SYCL_REORDER_EXPERTS (default: today)        \  live since
#   0013  a refused pool commit fails the request            }  2026-11-24 in
#   0014  a second termination signal leaves at once        /  9ea95e93a83c
#   0015  parking: weights that leave the card and come back at the same
#         addresses — OFF unless a model's env switches it on
#   0016  GGML_SYCL_POOL_REFUSE, the test of 0013's refusal — OFF
#   0017  the MoE cache filled from a record of the experts used — OFF
#         unless a model's env names the record's directory
# With every switch off it must gate as 9ea95e93a83c does, fingerprint for
# fingerprint, or it rolls back. The measurements then run on COPIES on this
# engine (docs/notes: parking-prototype.md §4, moe-expert-record.md §5,
# omnivoice-on-our-backend.md §13); no separate prototype engine is built.
